# Project: Flutter Cross-Platform App (iOS-first)

This document is the **source of truth** for the AI assistant (Claude Code). It describes
the architecture, stack, conventions, and platform priorities. In any conflict between
general Flutter rules and this file — **this file wins**.

## 1. Project context

- **Platform priority:** iOS/macOS → Android → Windows → Linux.
- **Backend:** Python and .NET, REST + gRPC. DTOs are shared via OpenAPI/protobuf.
- **Architectural approach:** Vertical Slice (each feature is split into slices) on top of
  Hexagonal (inside each slice — ports and adapters).
- **Framework goal:** a reusable template from which new applications will grow.
- **Minimum boilerplate in features, maximum in `core/`.**

## 2. Technology stack (locked)

| Area | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| State management | `flutter_bloc` 9.x (Cubit by default, Bloc — when event traceability is needed) | event-driven, maps well to hexagonal use-cases |
| Navigation | `auto_route` 9.x | type-safe, codegen, better for deeply nested navigation |
| Localization | `slang` + `slang_flutter` | type-safe i18n via codegen from JSON |
| DI | `get_it` + `injectable` | generated DI graph, easy to mock in tests |
| HTTP | `dio` + `retrofit` | codegen API clients from annotations |
| gRPC | `grpc` + `protobuf` | for .NET/Python backend |
| Serialization | `freezed` + `json_serializable` | sealed classes for states and models |
| Storage | `flutter_secure_storage` (secrets) + `hive`/`isar` (cache) | |
| Tests | `bloc_test` + `mocktail` + `flutter_test` | mocktail is preferred over mockito |
| Format | `dart format` + `very_good_analysis` lints | |

**Prohibited without explicit discussion:** `Provider`, `Riverpod`, `GetX`, `MobX`, `go_router`,
`mockito` (use mocktail), `json_annotation` without freezed, global singletons
outside `get_it`.

